load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A pseudovector: a quantity that transforms like a vector under rotations but flips sign under a reflection, where a
# true vector would not, because it is secretly an oriented area (a bivector) in disguise. Angular momentum and the
# magnetic field are pseudovectors. The distinction is exactly the even-versus-odd grading of the geometric algebra. The
# form carries the underlying vector space.
form pseudovector
  link space, like vector-space
